{"page_content": "Procedural and control technologies used to minimise residual emissions/exposure. Qualitative/quantit Residual ative risk exposure considerations for information residual exposures/emissio ns. Risk considerations Local Exhaust Ventilation. Exhaust emissions are incinerated. PPE/RPE are worn as good practice. Negligible dermal exposure possible but unlikely. The substance has a low vapour pressure and low water solubility and can be collected using absorbing material if spilled. No emission to the air or water environment is foreseen. No release to the environment is expected during the four life cycle stages. The main waste stream is as hazardous waste which is treated by incineration.", "metadata": {"doc_id": "f08f8b2b-6edc-4a66-9cf6-35c811162949", "content_type": "Table", "filename": "information_requirements_r5_en.pdf"}}